  "main_text": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is Raj Sanchez with user ID raj_sanchez_7340. He wants to cancel a reservation from Philadelphia to LaGuardia. He mentioned that a customer support rep told him a service agent can help, and if they say it can't be canceled, he wants to reference that approval. Also, he doesn't want to proceed without a refund.\n\nFirst, I need to check the reservation details. To do that, I need the reservation ID. But the user hasn't provided it. So, I should get his user details to find the reservation. The function get_user_details requires the user_id. Let me call that first. \n\nOnce I have the user details, I can look for the reservation that matches the Philadelphia to LaGuardia trip. Then, I need to check the status of the flights in that reservation. If any flight has already departed, cancellation isn't possible. If not, I can proceed. \n\nBut wait, the user hasn't given the reservation ID. So the first step is to retrieve his user details to find the relevant reservation. Let me start by calling get_user_details with his user ID.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_user_details\", \"arguments\": {\"user_id\": \"raj_sanchez_7340\"}}\n",
